index 0000000..97d2c54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-expose-post-search-and-creation-to-ai-assistants-over-mcp.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/PostPolicy.ts
+generated: { by: "human:Urata Daiki", at: 2026-09-25T05:20:46.185Z }
+---
+
+# Expose post search and creation to AI assistants over MCP
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write with their own AI assistants and want them to search what is
+already published and draft new posts without copying text back and forth. We
+do not want a chatbot in the blog, and we do not want a second implementation
+of search or post creation to keep in step with the website.
+
+## Decision
+
+- The existing `posts.search` (QUERY) and `posts.store` (POST) routes carry
+  `.agent()` metadata and are served as the MCP tools `posts_search` and
+  `posts_store` by `@guren/plugin-mcp` at `/mcp`. Tool names use underscores
+  because some clients drop names containing a dot.
+- Input rules, validation and the `PostPolicy` check are the route's own; the
+  tool has no schema or permission logic of its own. `posts_store` always takes
+  the author from the authenticated user.
+- `/mcp` accepts bearer tokens only, verified against the `api_tokens` table
+  through `DatabaseApiTokenStore` (`AuthProvider`). Ops issue tokens from a
+  terminal; there is no self-service page yet.
+- `PostController.store` answers a JSON-accepting, non-Inertia request with
+  the created post so the tool result is typed; browser forms keep the
+  redirect.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- One implementation serves the site and assistants; a change to the schema
+  or the policy reaches both.
+- Editing and deleting posts, approval of tool calls, audit logging and
+  self-service token management stay out of scope until requested.
